          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called the
            %em Feynman propagator
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetime"} globally hyperbolic spacetime
            is one of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+functions"} Green functions
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo □
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box + m^2
            (hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+solution"} fundamental solution
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equation"} wave equation
            when the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            vanishes).
          %p
            As discussed in detail at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "S-matrix#ExistenceAndRenormalization"} S-matrix – Feynman diagrams and renormalization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            (in the same way as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
            encodes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+ordered+products"} normal ordered products
            of quantum fields). This implies that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"} scattering amplitude
            associated with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagram"} Feynman diagram
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+perturbation+series"} Feynman perturbation series
            expansion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            is, away from the locus of coinciding interaction points, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product
            of Feynman propagators, one for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge"} edge
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagram"} Feynman diagram
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+distributions"} extension of distributions
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
            to coinciding points is
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
          %p
            This is why Feynman propagators are ubiquituous in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            By the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "S-matrix#ExistenceAndRenormalization"} S-matrix – Feynman diagrams and renormalization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_F
            is properly defined to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
            of the chosen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
            (encoding the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+state"} vacuum state
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+causal+propagator"} advanced causal propagator
          #FeynmanPropatorAsSumOfHadamardPropagatorWithAdvancedPropagator.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (Feynman propagator on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetimes"} globally hyperbolic spacetimes
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time+orientation"} time-oriented
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetime"} globally hyperbolic spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              there exists a unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+causal+propagator"} advanced causal propagator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_A \in \mathcal{D}'(\Sigma \times \Sigma)
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \mathcal{D}'(\Sigma \times \Sigma)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              (the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+state"} vacuum state
              %em Feynman propagator
              is the sum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi F
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi ω
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega_F \coloneqq \omega + i \Delta_A
                    \\,.
          %p
            (for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            this is e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Scharf95"} Scharf 95 (2.3.41)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetimes"} globally hyperbolic spacetimes
            this is
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Radzikowski96"} Radzikowski 96, p. 5
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            this may be expressed as a sum of
