          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+distribution"} Hadamard distribution
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+propagator"} Chern-Simons propagator
          %h2#references References
          %p Analytical aspects of special generalized functions associated to quadratic forms are given in
          %ul
            %li#GelfandShilov66
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Israel+M.+Gelfand"}> Israel M. Gelfand
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georgiy+E.+Shilov"} Georgiy E. Shilov
              %em Generalized Functions
              Vol. 1 (1958), Acad. Press (1966-1968), AMS (2016) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=CHELGELFSET"}> ISBN:978-1-4704-2885-3
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Textbook accounts for quantum fields on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Scharf95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%BCnter+Scharf"}> Günter Scharf
                , section 2.3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Finite+Quantum+Electrodynamics+--+The+Causal+Approach"} Finite Quantum Electrodynamics – The Causal Approach
            %li#Scharf01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%BCnter+Scharf"}> Günter Scharf
                , section 1 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Gauge+Theories+--+A+True+Ghost+Story"} Quantum Gauge Theories – A True Ghost Story
            %li#DeWitt03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bryce+DeWitt"}> Bryce DeWitt
                ,
                %em The global approach to Quantum Field Theory
                (2 volumes), Oxford 2003
          %p
            An concise overview of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+functions"} Green functions
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+propagator"} advanced propagator
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retarded+propagator"} retarded propagator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
            etc. is given in
          %ul
            %li#Kocic16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikica+Kocic"}> Mikica Kocic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Invariant Commutation and Propagation Functions Invariant Commutation and Propagation Functions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KGPropagatorsOnMinkowskiTable.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion on general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetimes"} globally hyperbolic spacetimes
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Radzikowski96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marek+Radzikowski"}> Marek Radzikowski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Micro-local approach to the Hadamard condition in quantum field theory on curved space-time
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104287114"} Euclid
          %p
            where the issue with the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagators"} Wightman propagators
            was settled, and reviewed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#BCEMZ03
              A. Bytsenko, G. Cognola,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emilio+Elizalde"} Emilio Elizalde
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valter+Moretti"} Valter Moretti
              = succeed "," do
                %em Analytic Aspects of Quantum Fields
          %p Lecture notes (mostly for the case over Minkowski spacetime) include
          %ul
            %li#Grozin05
              %p
                Andrey Grozin,
                %em Lectures on QED and QCD
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0508242"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0508242
                )
            %li#GFP
              %p
                %em Green functions and propagators
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GreenFunctionsAndPropagators.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %em Green functions for the Klein-Gordon operator
                (
                %a{:href => "http://sgovindarajan.wdfiles.com/local--files/serc2009/greenfunction.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Kleinert11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hagen+Kleinert"}> Hagen Kleinert
                , V. Schulte-Frohlinde,
                %em
                  Critical properties of
                  = succeed "-Theories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^4
                2001 (
                %a{:href => "http://users.physik.fu-berlin.de/~kleinert/b8/psfiles/08.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            An overview of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green+functions"} Green functions
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+propagator"} advanced propagator
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retarded+propagator"} retarded propagator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
            etc. is given in
          %ul
            %li#Kocic16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikica+Kocic"}> Mikica Kocic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Invariant Commutation and Propagation Functions Invariant Commutation and Propagation Functions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KGPropagatorsOnMinkowskiTable.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p The zeta function regularization method originates around
          %ul
            %li#Speer71
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugene+Speer"}> Eugene Speer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the structure of Analytic Renormalization
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103857549"} Euclid
          %p
            and a comprehensive discussion is in (
            %a{:href => "#BCEMZ03"}> BCEMZ 03, section 2
            ).
          %p Discussion of zeta functions of Dirac operators in 2d includes
          %ul
            %li
              Michael McGuigan,
              %em Riemann Hypothesis and Short Distance Fermionic Green’s Functions
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0504035"}> arXiv:math-ph/0504035
              )
          %p
            Lecture notes concerning 1-loop vacuum amplitudes for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            include
          %ul
            %li
              %em The IIA/B superstring one-loop vacuum amplitude
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.thphys.uni-heidelberg.de/~palti/Stringcourse/problemset11.pdf"}> pdf
              )
